  "comment": "Three flat grey bands on a layer of their own. Levels from the Filter menu draws each as a bar, and so does Curves. Each eyedropper is armed by its button and a real click on a band moves the black point, the gamma or the white point. Escape puts an armed one away and leaves the dialog open. Equalize reads pressed with a caption naming its channel, and Reset raises the button and dims the caption. Then Levels attached to the layer and edited in Tool Options: each pick is one Edit Filter step, and Ctrl+Z takes them back one at a time."
